From 8d5ad7517ca6545019de6a116f29db13dac088cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:41:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 42/58] sniff: bounded, panic-safe, buffers given back

The CRYPTO frames of a QUIC Initial are bounded, the TLS server handshake stops once the ClientHello
is captured, a panicking sniffer fails its connection (its stack logged once a minute), a datagram
that is no DNS query goes on to the other sniffers, a WireGuard handshake is not uTP, and the
sniffed buffers are given back when matching fails.

Made of these commits of the earlier series (branch archive/r25-1.14-commits):
  32ed14311 sniff: bound the CRYPTO frames of a QUIC Initial
  755441478 sniff: stop the TLS server handshake once the ClientHello is captured
  15bb66148 sniff: a panicking sniffer fails its connection, a UDP sniff reads 16 packets
  88f612717 sniff: log the stack of a panicking sniffer once a minute, not per connection
  8ca515541 sniff: a datagram that is no DNS query goes on to the other packet sniffers
  4bba622d9 route: give back the sniffed buffers when matching the rules fails
  e433f648e sniff: a WireGuard handshake initiation is not uTP

Pdk-Feature: sniff
Pdk-Zone: core
Pdk-Layer: 04
